{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>May He give you.</b> He will give and give again (Bereshit Rabbah). And according to its plain sense it refers back to the first matter: ״See, the smell of my son״ — which the Holy One, blessed be He, gave him as ״the smell of a field״ etc. — and He will yet give you of the dew of the heavens etc." "<b>Of the dew of the heavens.</b> As it sounds; and there are many facets in its midrashic aggadah." "<b>The Elohim.</b> What is ״the Eloheim״? Justice — if you are worthy He will give you, and if not, He will not give you. But to Esav He said, ״of the fatnesses of the earth shall be your dwelling״ — whether righteous or wicked He will give you. And from it Solomon learned: when he built the House he arranged his prayer accordingly. Israel, who is a master of faith and who justifies the decree upon himself — ״he will not call a claim against you״; therefore ״וְנָתַתָּ לָאִישׁ בְּכָל דְּרָכָיו אֲשֶׁר תֵּדַע אֶת לְבָבוֹ״ (I Kings 8). But a gentile lacks faith; therefore he said ״אַתָּה תִּשְׁמַע הַשָּׁמָיִם״, ״וְעָשִׂיתָ כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָא אֵלֶיךָ הַנָּכְרִי״ (ibid.) — whether worthy or not worthy, give him, so that he will not call a claim against you."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:50.593686678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}